# set(v) { this.bump(); } .. target[KEY] = 1: nobody else calls bump()
# `target` is an instance of Row that has not escaped; the same place also sees an object that took descriptors out of JSON.parse(), whose accessor under the key may be anything. The accessor of the program lies on that object too, so it has escaped, and `unknown` stands for it in what the lookup answers.
# The store under a key that nobody knows enters it with the instance all the same.
